{number: 10}
{title: O Worship the King}
{key: Ab}

{start_of_verse: 1}
[Ab] O worship the King, all glorious above,
O [Eb] gratefully sing His [Ab] wonderful love;
Our [Ab] Shield and De-[Eb] fender, the [Ab] Ancient of [Db] days,
Pa-[Ab] vilioned in splendor, and [Eb7] girded with [Ab] praise.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 2}
[Ab] O tell of His might, and sing of His grace,
Whose [Eb] robe is the light, whose [Ab] canopy space;
His [Ab] chariots of [Eb] wrath the deep [Ab] thunderclouds [Db] form,
And [Ab] dark is His path on the [Eb7] wings of the [Ab] storm.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
[Ab] Thy bountiful care what tongue can recite?
It [Eb] breathes in the air, it [Ab] shines in the light,
It [Ab] streams from the [Eb] hills, it de-[Ab] scends to the [Db] plain,
And [Ab] sweetly distills in the [Eb7] dew and the [Ab] rain.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 4}
[Ab] Frail children of dust, and feeble as frail,
In [Eb] Thee do we trust, nor [Ab] find Thee to fail;
Thy [Ab] mercies how [Eb] tender! how [Ab] firm to the [Db] end!
Our [Ab] Maker, Defender, Re-[Eb7] deemer, and [Ab] Friend.
{end_of_verse}
